WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.339
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:08.816
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:17.573
Unit twenty-six: Gerund and Infinitive: Advanced Patterns. Today you will recognise verbs whose meaning changes with the form.

4
00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:20.491
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:24.434
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:26.551
Remember doing.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.979
Remember doing means recall a past action.

8
00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:32.130
I remember meeting her.

9
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:35.636
Your turn. Say: Remember doing.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.873
Remember doing.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.792
Regret to say.

12
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:45.955
Regret to say means to say something sad or formal.

13
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.584
I regret to say we are closed.

14
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:52.683
Your turn. Say: Regret to say.

15
00:00:55.533 --> 00:00:57.092
Regret to say.

16
00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:58.839
Go on doing.

17
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.233
Go on doing means to continue an action.

18
00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:04.212
She went on talking.

19
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:07.690
Your turn. Say: Go on doing.

20
00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:11.767
Go on doing.

21
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:13.587
Go on to do.

22
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.012
Go on to do means to move to a next action.

23
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:18.954
He went on to win.

24
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.307
Your turn. Say: Go on to do.

25
00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.319
Go on to do.

26
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:27.957
Mean doing.

27
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.565
Mean doing means to involve or result in.

28
00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.430
This means waiting.

29
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:36.832
Your turn. Say: Mean doing.

30
00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.784
Mean doing.

31
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.505
Mean to do.

32
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:45.238
Mean to do means to intend.

33
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.165
I meant to call you.

34
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.309
Your turn. Say: Mean to do.

35
00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.226
Mean to do.

36
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:56.298
Can't help doing.

37
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.643
Can't help doing means cannot stop yourself.

38
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.774
I can't help laughing.

39
00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:05.384
Your turn. Say: Can't help doing.

40
00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:09.641
Can't help doing.

41
00:02:10.383 --> 00:02:11.466
Meaning change.

42
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.506
Meaning change means a different sense with another form.

43
00:02:16.117 --> 00:02:17.420
A meaning change.

44
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:20.982
Your turn. Say: Meaning change.

45
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:24.962
Meaning change.

46
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:29.499
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:35.078
Visal, what is the difference between I remember to post it and I remember posting it?

48
00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:47.035
Remember to post is an action you do not forget. Remember posting is a memory of a past action. The same pattern applies to forget, stop and try.

49
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.581
Which others are tricky?

50
00:02:50.683 --> 00:03:06.179
Go on doing means continue, while go on to do means do the next thing. Mean to do is to intend, and mean doing is to involve. Regret to say is formal news, but regret saying is sorrow about the past.

51
00:03:07.283 --> 00:03:08.401
And can't help?

52
00:03:09.517 --> 00:03:22.212
Can't help + gerund means cannot stop oneself: I can't help laughing. Learn these pairs one at a time, with your own examples, because the meaning depends entirely on the form.

53
00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.192
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:33.170
Grammar focus: Verb plus gerund (past, continuing) vs verb plus to-infinitive (next, intended).

55
00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.610
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:35.317 --> 00:03:37.374
I remember meeting her years ago.

57
00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:39.842
He went on to win the final.

58
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.842
I can't help laughing at his jokes.

59
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:52.968
Some verbs change meaning: remember, regret, go on, mean, stop, try. Gerund = past / continuing. To-infinitive = next / intended.

60
00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:57.449
Be careful! Don't say: I remember to meet her once.

61
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.469
Say: I remember meeting her once.

62
00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:03.513
Use the gerund for memory.

63
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.382
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.946
Same Verb, Different Meaning.

65
00:04:10.246 --> 00:04:13.441
I remember meeting my best friend on the first day of school.

66
00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:16.665
I must remember to send her a card.

67
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.469
She went on talking for an hour.

68
00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.826
He went on to become a famous scientist.

69
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:26.657
I can't help smiling when I see old photos.

70
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.931
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:32.783 --> 00:04:34.597
I remember blank him last year.

72
00:04:34.897 --> 00:04:37.947
A, meeting. B, to meet. C, meet.

73
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.349
The answer is A: meeting.

74
00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:47.263
Remember blank the door! (do not forget)

75
00:04:47.563 --> 00:04:50.718
A, locking. B, to lock. C, lock.

76
00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.953
The answer is B: to lock.

77
00:04:57.117 --> 00:04:59.757
She went on blank a doctor. (next step)

78
00:05:00.057 --> 00:05:03.560
A, becoming. B, to become. C, become.

79
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.018
The answer is B: to become.

80
00:05:10.183 --> 00:05:11.510
I can't help blank.

81
00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.149
A, laugh. B, laughing. C, to laugh.

82
00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.862
The answer is B: laughing.

83
00:05:22.017 --> 00:05:25.073
According to the reading, what must the writer remember to send?

84
00:05:25.373 --> 00:05:28.968
A, a card. B, a letter. C, a gift.

85
00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:34.359
The answer is A: a card.

86
00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.881
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:39.717 --> 00:05:43.702
Write two sentences that show the difference between 'go on doing' and 'go on to do'.

88
00:05:52.517 --> 00:05:53.959
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:54.259 --> 00:06:05.645
He went on talking for two hours, so we were tired. He went on to become a famous writer after he finished school. The first means continue, and the second means the next step.

90
00:06:05.945 --> 00:06:07.782
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:08.683 --> 00:06:17.524
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb plus gerund (past, continuing) vs verb plus to-infinitive (next, intended).

92
00:06:17.824 --> 00:06:22.775
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:23.075 --> 00:06:26.552
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:29.783
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

